ISHA – Local AI Backend Replacement & Ultra-Fast Response Update

Mujhe existing ISHA project me ek major local-AI backend update karna hai.

1. Main Objective

Existing ISHA me jo Ollama/local model integration hai, usko completely remove/replace karna hai.

Uski jagah direct GGUF model inference using llama.cpp / llama-cpp-python use karna hai.

Reason:

- Ollama response dene me noticeable delay kar raha hai.
- Mere standalone GGUF test code me response noticeably fast aa raha hai.
- Mere "gguf.py" implementation me "llama_cpp.Llama" ke through GGUF load ho raha hai.
- Usme "create_chat_completion(..., stream=True)" use karke response token/chunk-by-chunk immediately print ho raha hai.
- ISHA me bhi isi type ka fast streaming behavior chahiye.

Mera goal hai ki ISHA ka local model direct GGUF ho aur response latency minimum ho.

---

2. Existing Ollama Backend Remove/Replace

Existing ISHA architecture me:

"ISHA → Ollama → Local Model → Response"

ko replace karke:

"ISHA → llama.cpp → GGUF Model → Streaming Response"

banana hai.

Ollama ko local inference ke liye dependency ke roop me use nahi karna hai.

Important:

- Ollama process start/stop/check karne wala unnecessary code remove karo.
- Ollama API calls remove karo.
- Ollama model names/configuration ko GGUF configuration se replace karo.
- Ollama unavailable/error handling ko GGUF/llama.cpp error handling se replace karo.
- Existing GUI ko redesign mat karo.
- Existing ISHA features ko unnecessarily remove mat karo.

---

3. GGUF Backend

Mere existing "gguf.py" code ko reference implementation ke roop me use karo.

Us code me:

from llama_cpp import Llama

ke through model load ho raha hai.

Model configuration approximately isi architecture par honi chahiye:

llm = Llama(
    model_path="MODEL_PATH.gguf",
    n_ctx=2048,
    n_threads=6,
    verbose=False
)

Lekin hard-coded values blindly copy mat karo.

System ke hardware ke according practical configuration provide karo.

GGUF model path configurable hona chahiye.

Example:

models/
    llama-3.2-3b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf

ya user-selected GGUF path.

GUI/configuration se model select/change karne ka option existing architecture ke according preserve karo.

---

4. Most Important: Streaming Response

Mere "gguf.py" me response streaming already fast hai.

Reference behavior:

response_stream = llm.create_chat_completion(
    messages=messages,
    temperature=0.7,
    max_tokens=256,
    stream=True
)

Aur chunks immediately process hote hain:

for chunk in response_stream:
    delta = chunk["choices"][0]["delta"]

    if "content" in delta:
        content = delta["content"]
        print(content, end="", flush=True)

ISHA me bhi exactly isi concept ko implement karo.

Response ko complete generate hone ke baad ek saath GUI me show mat karo.

Instead:

"GGUF generates token"
↓
"token/chunk immediately received"
↓
"GUI text area immediately updated"
↓
"TTS ko bhi immediately streamed text milta rahe"

---

5. GUI Text Display ko Fast Karo

ISHA ke GUI me jo AI response text print/show hota hai, usme currently unnecessary delay hai.

Usko optimize karo.

Required behavior:

Jaise hi GGUF se response ka first token/chunk aaye:

GUI me immediately show hona chahiye.

User ko model ka complete answer generate hone ka wait nahi karna chahiye.

Example:

Model internally generate kar raha hai:

Hello

GUI:

Hello

Next chunk:

Hello! How

GUI immediately update:

Hello! How

Next:

Hello! How can I

GUI immediately update.

Is tarah response live stream hona chahiye.

---

6. GUI Thread Freeze Nahi Hona Chahiye

Important:

GGUF inference GUI/main thread me directly run mat karo agar usse GUI freeze hota hai.

Architecture:

GUI/Main Thread
       |
       | User message
       ↓
AI Worker Thread
       |
       ↓
llama.cpp / GGUF
       |
       | streaming chunks
       ↓
GUI Signal/Event
       |
       ↓
Text Display

AI generation background worker/thread me chale.

GUI responsive rahe.

User simultaneously:

- scrolling kar sake
- buttons use kar sake
- stop generation kar sake
- new UI interactions kar sake

---

7. GUI Text Update Optimization

Har single character ke liye expensive GUI operation mat karo agar usse performance reduce hoti hai.

Streaming ko optimize karo.

Possible architecture:

GGUF chunk
   ↓
small text buffer
   ↓
very frequent lightweight GUI update
   ↓
display

Lekin buffering itni large nahi honi chahiye ki visible delay aaye.

Goal:

Fast + smooth streaming

na ki:

Generate complete response → suddenly display everything

---

8. Text-to-Speech ko Response ke Saath Start Karo

Ye second major update hai.

Currently TTS response complete hone ke baad start ho raha hai, jiski wajah se user ko extra wait karna padta hai.

Is behavior ko change karo.

Current:

User
 ↓
GGUF generates complete answer
 ↓
GUI displays complete answer
 ↓
TTS starts

Required:

User
 ↓
GGUF starts
 ↓
First text chunks
 ↓
GUI immediately displays
 ↓
TTS simultaneously starts/queues speech
 ↓
GGUF continues generating
 ↓
GUI continues streaming
 ↓
TTS continues speaking

---

9. TTS Must Work Parallel to Generation

TTS ko blocking operation mat banao.

Agar TTS synchronous hai aur model generation ko block karta hai, architecture incorrect hoga.

Required:

                ┌──→ GUI Streaming
GGUF Stream ────┤
                └──→ TTS Queue

TTS ka separate worker/thread/queue use karo.

Model ko TTS ke complete hone ka wait nahi karna chahiye.

Example:

GGUF generates:

Hello! Welcome to ISHA.

Jaise hi enough natural speech text available ho:

TTS:

Hello! Welcome to ISHA.

bolna start kare.

Meanwhile GGUF next text generate karta rahe.

---

10. TTS ko Character-by-Character Mat Bolo

Har individual token/character ko TTS me send karna bad implementation hoga.

Speech ko natural chunks me divide karo.

Best approach:

Sentence/chunk based TTS queue

Example:

GGUF stream:
"Hello! Welcome to ISHA. How can I help you today?"

TTS chunks:

"Hello! Welcome to ISHA."

then:

"How can I help you today?"

Jaise hi sentence/appropriate phrase complete ho, usko TTS queue me daal do.

TTS previous chunk bol raha ho aur GGUF next chunk generate kar raha ho.

---

11. TTS First-Speech Latency Reduce Karo

Important optimization:

TTS ko poora AI response complete hone tak wait nahi karna hai.

First natural sentence/chunk complete hote hi TTS start hona chahiye.

Target architecture:

First sentence generated
        ↓
GUI shows it
        ↓
TTS queue receives it
        ↓
TTS starts

Meanwhile:

GGUF → next sentence

generate karta rahe.

---

12. TTS Queue

Dedicated TTS queue implement karo.

Example architecture:

GGUF Worker
     |
     | text chunk
     ↓
TTS Queue
     |
     ↓
TTS Worker
     |
     ↓
Speech Output

TTS Worker ko model worker se independent rakho.

Agar TTS slow hai, model generation slow nahi hona chahiye.

---

13. TTS Engine Existing Implementation Preserve Karo

ISHA me jo existing TTS engines available hain unhe unnecessarily remove mat karo.

Agar project me multiple TTS fallback already hai, us architecture ko preserve karte hue streaming/queue behavior add karo.

Priority:

1. Existing preferred TTS
2. Existing fallback
3. Existing system/native TTS

Lekin TTS ko asynchronous banana important hai.

---

14. Stop Button

Agar ISHA me Stop/Cancel generation functionality already hai, usko GGUF streaming ke saath integrate karo.

User Stop press kare to:

GGUF generation stop
+
TTS queue clear
+
Current TTS stop/cancel if supported

hona chahiye.

Old queued sentences ko Stop ke baad speak nahi karna chahiye.

---

15. Conversation Memory

Existing conversation/history system ko preserve karo.

GGUF ko messages isi type ke structured format me bhejo:

messages = [
    {"role": "system", "content": "..."},
    {"role": "user", "content": "..."}
]

Assistant ka final collected response history me save karo:

{"role": "assistant", "content": collected_text}

Streaming ke dauran GUI update alag ho sakta hai, lekin final complete response conversation memory me correctly save hona chahiye.

---

16. ISHA Personality/System Prompt

GGUF ko clearly pata hona chahiye ki:

- Ye ISHA ke andar running local AI hai.
- Model ISHA ka brain hai.
- OS/tool layer ISHA ke actions/hands hain.
- Existing ISHA tools/action system ke through permitted operations perform karne hain.

Existing ISHA system prompt/personality ko preserve karo.

Ollama-specific assumptions ko remove karke GGUF-compatible prompt flow banao.

---

17. Existing ISHA Tool/OS System Preserve Karo

Important:

Sirf Ollama replace karna hai.

ISHA ke existing:

- PC control
- file operations
- system monitoring
- browser operations
- memory
- TTS
- STT
- GUI
- tools
- permissions
- confirmations
- security
- logging

ko unnecessarily remove mat karo.

GGUF ko existing ISHA orchestration/tool system ke saath connect karo.

Architecture:

                 ┌── GUI
                 │
User → ISHA → GGUF Brain
                 │
                 ├── Memory
                 │
                 ├── Tool/Action Layer
                 │
                 ├── OS Control
                 │
                 └── TTS

---

18. Model Configuration

GUI/config me possible configuration provide karo:

GGUF Model
Model Path
Context Size
CPU Threads
GPU Layers (if supported)
Temperature
Max Tokens

Lekin existing GUI design ko unnecessarily change mat karo.

Agar existing model/backend settings screen hai, usi me GGUF settings integrate karo.

---

19. CPU/GPU Optimization

"llama-cpp-python" ke available capabilities ke according hardware acceleration support rakho.

CPU mode:

n_threads = appropriate CPU thread count

GPU support available ho to configurable GPU layers use karne ka option rakho.

Hard-code hardware assumptions mat karo.

App start hone par model unnecessarily repeatedly reload nahi hona chahiye.

---

20. Model Loading

GGUF model ko application startup par preferably ek baar load karo.

Har user message par:

load model
generate
unload model

aisa nahi hona chahiye.

Instead:

ISHA Start
 ↓
GGUF Model Load
 ↓
Model stays loaded
 ↓
User message
 ↓
Fast generation

Isse repeated model-loading latency avoid hogi.

---

21. First Response Latency

Model load hone ke baad first token tak ka delay minimum karne ke liye existing GGUF configuration optimize karo.

Generation ke waqt unnecessary:

- file operations
- network calls
- Ollama health checks
- unnecessary logging
- blocking TTS
- unnecessary GUI refresh
- model reload

avoid karo.

---

22. No Ollama Dependency

Final implementation me local inference ke liye:

Ollama = NOT REQUIRED

hona chahiye.

ISHA directly:

llama-cpp-python
+
GGUF

use kare.

Agar Ollama installed nahi hai tab bhi local GGUF AI work karna chahiye.

---

23. Error Handling

GGUF model missing ho:

GGUF model not found.
Please select/configure a valid GGUF model.

jaisa clear GUI error dikhao.

"llama_cpp" missing ho to clear dependency error do.

Invalid model path ho to application crash nahi karni chahiye.

TTS fail ho to:

AI generation continue honi chahiye.

TTS failure se GGUF generation stop nahi honi chahiye.

---

24. Performance Logging

Optional lightweight performance metrics add karo:

Model load time
Time to first token
Tokens/sec
Total generation time
TTS start latency

Debug mode me ye information useful hogi.

Normal GUI me unnecessary debug spam mat dikhao.

---

25. Required Final Flow

Final ISHA response pipeline:

USER INPUT
    ↓
ISHA GUI
    ↓
GGUF / llama.cpp
    ↓
STREAMING TOKENS
    ↓
    ├──────────────→ GUI TEXT DISPLAY
    │                    ↓
    │              User sees response
    │              immediately
    │
    └──────────────→ TTS TEXT BUFFER
                         ↓
                   Sentence detected
                         ↓
                    TTS QUEUE
                         ↓
                    TTS WORKER
                         ↓
                    SPEECH OUTPUT

All of these processes should run without unnecessarily blocking each other.

---

26. Performance Goal

Main objective:

ISHA ko mere existing "gguf.py" test code ke streaming behavior ke jitna responsive banana hai.

Reference implementation me:

stream=True

use karke generated content immediately print hota hai.

ISHA GUI me bhi same low-latency streaming behavior chahiye.

Goal:

User sends message
        ↓
GGUF starts generation
        ↓
First token/chunk
        ↓
GUI immediately displays
        ↓
TTS begins when first natural speech chunk is ready
        ↓
Remaining response continues streaming
        ↓
GUI + TTS work in parallel

---

27. Important: Don't Break Existing GUI

Existing ISHA GUI/design ko completely redesign mat karo.

Preserve:

- current window
- current layout
- current buttons
- current styling
- current chat interface
- current controls

Sirf backend aur response pipeline ko optimize/replace karo.

---

28. Code Quality

Implementation clean modular architecture me karo.

Suggested separation:

GGUFEngine
    ↓
StreamingGenerator
    ↓
ResponseHandler
    ├── GUI Stream
    └── TTS Stream

Possible classes/modules:

GGUFModelManager
GGUFInferenceWorker
StreamingResponseHandler
TTSWorker
TTSQueue

Existing project architecture ke according names adjust kar sakte ho.

Duplicate code create mat karo.

---

29. Do Not Do This

❌ Ollama ko GGUF ke saath unnecessary parallel backend mat rakho.

❌ Full response generate hone ke baad GUI me print mat karo.

❌ Full response complete hone ke baad TTS start mat karo.

❌ TTS ko main generation thread me blocking mat rakho.

❌ Har token ko separate TTS request mat banao.

❌ Har character par expensive GUI redraw mat karo.

❌ Har message par GGUF model reload mat karo.

❌ Existing ISHA tools/features ko sirf backend change ke naam par remove mat karo.

❌ GUI ko unnecessary redesign mat karo.

---

30. Testing Required

Implementation complete karne ke baad ye tests karo:

Test 1 – Basic Chat

User:

Hello ISHA

Check:

- GGUF response
- streaming
- GUI immediate output
- TTS

Test 2 – Long Response

A moderately long question ask karo.

Check:

- GUI continuously streams
- GUI freeze nahi hota
- TTS response ke saath start hota hai
- TTS aur generation ek dusre ko block nahi karte

Test 3 – Stop

Generation ke beech Stop press karo.

Check:

- generation stops
- TTS queue clears
- old queued speech continue nahi hoti

Test 4 – Model Missing

Invalid GGUF path do.

Check:

- clear error
- application crash nahi

Test 5 – TTS Failure

TTS unavailable hone par check karo:

- GGUF still works
- GUI still streams
- app crash nahi hota

Test 6 – Existing ISHA Tools

Existing tool/action system ka test karo.

Check:

GGUF Brain
    ↓
ISHA Orchestrator
    ↓
Tool Layer
    ↓
Result
    ↓
GGUF
    ↓
Streaming final response

---

31. Final Requirement

Mujhe ISHA me Ollama-based local AI nahi chahiye.

Mujhe:

Direct GGUF + llama.cpp based local AI

chahiye.

Aur response system:

Fast streaming GUI + parallel low-latency TTS

hona chahiye.

Final architecture:

              ISHA
                │
                ▼
        GGUF / llama.cpp
          (ISHA Brain)
                │
        Streaming Output
          ┌─────┴─────┐
          ▼           ▼
      GUI Text      TTS Queue
          │           │
          ▼           ▼
    Live Response  TTS Worker
                      │
                      ▼
                    Voice

Mere uploaded "gguf.py" ko reference implementation for fast GGUF streaming ke roop me use karo. Usme existing "Llama(...)" loading aur "create_chat_completion(..., stream=True)" behavior ko ISHA ke architecture me properly integrate karo.

Sabse important priorities:

1. Ollama remove/replace
2. Direct GGUF inference
3. Fast first-token response
4. Live GUI streaming
5. GUI non-blocking
6. TTS response generation ke saath parallel
7. Sentence/chunk-based TTS queue
8. Existing ISHA GUI/features preserve
9. Existing tools/OS integration preserve
10. Overall response latency minimum